# Niv-Mizzet, Guildpact (5/5 colors, 6/6 flying): "Whenever Niv-Mizzet deals combat damage to a player, it deals X damage to any target, target player
# draws X cards, and you gain X life, where X is the number of different color pairs among permanents you control that are exactly two colors"
# (CR 510.2, 603.2, 105.1). Bot1 controls Watchwolf (green-white) and Spike Jester (black-red) on turn 3: two different pairs, so X is 2, and Niv
# itself (five colors) does not count. Bot2's Memnite cannot block the flyer (CR 702.9). Niv deals 6 combat damage and the trigger deals 2 more to
# Bot2 (20 -> 12), Bot1 draws exactly two cards and gains 2 (20 -> 22).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Niv-Mizzet, Guildpact
Watchwolf
Spike Jester
Plains x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Niv-Mizzet, Guildpact.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Watchwolf.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spike Jester.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Niv-Mizzet, Guildpact > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Memnite > Niv-Mizzet, Guildpact)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 12
Bot1.Life = 22
Bot1.Hand.Count = 2
